# 0022 — restore the wasm-port edits that dreamcast/flycast-src had LOST
#
# WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS. dreamcast/flycast-src/ is gitignored in its entirety
# (.gitignore:60 — `git ls-files dreamcast/flycast-src` returns 0 of its 1,834
# .cpp files), so nothing in this repo records its contents and nothing warns
# when it drifts. It drifted: eight files silently reverted to a pre-wasm-port
# state, and because the SHIPPED flycast_worker_emcc.wasm predated the drift,
# the damage was invisible until someone tried to relink. Every relink from
# 2026-09-04 onward produced a worker that booted PSO to two frames and then
# died; `git log` showed nothing because git cannot see this tree.
#
# THE TWO EDITS THAT ACTUALLY KILLED THE BOOT (the rest are correctness/perf):
#
#   core/emulator.cpp  Emulator::start() — config::ThreadedRendering.override(false)
#     Without it flycast takes the ThreadedRendering branch and spawns its own
#     std::async SH4 thread, which races the worker's own dispatch pump.
#
#   core/hw/sh4/dyna/ssa.cpp — disable the read-only const-fold on WASM
#     The fold's safety depends on page-fault SMC, which wasm does not have, so
#     PSO's interrupt dispatcher froze its latched INTEVT word at 0x320 (VBlank)
#     and every interrupt — including Maple 0x360 — routed to the VBlank
#     handler. Maple bit12 never got acked => re-vector storm, the guest stopped
#     submitting frames, and the renderer's 20 ms wait turned into an ASYNCIFY
#     suspension that unwound out of retro_run as a bare `unwind` exception.
#
# THE REAL SOURCE OF TRUTH IS NOT THIS PATCH. It is the sibling checkout at
#   /Users/caseybement/Dev/dreamcastHtml/dreamcast/flycast-src
# (the "source repo" that commit 9441581f says this tree was synced from). This
# patch is a REPLAY of one recovery and will rot. To check for drift, diff the
# trees directly — it takes seconds and is exact:
#
#   diff -rq -x "build-*" -x .git -x .DS_Store \
#     dreamcast/flycast-src /Users/caseybement/Dev/dreamcastHtml/dreamcast/flycast-src
#
# Anything but `core/version.h` (a generated build stamp) is drift. Do that
# BEFORE trusting any relink, and prefer syncing the named files from the
# reference over replaying patches: `patch --dry-run` LIED about this tree in
# both directions (BSD patch skips already-applied hunks and still exits 0, and
# fuzz matched a FEAT_AREC hunk against the wrong one of build.h's four
# identical `#define FEAT_AREC DYNAREC_NONE` lines).
#
# Baseline for this patch = the tree as found on 2026-09-07. Files covered:
#   core/build.h                  FEAT_AREC DYNAREC_JIT (0020 hunk; the whole
#                                 ARM7 wasm dynarec was compiling out)
#   core/emulator.cpp             single-threaded pin (BOOT-CRITICAL)
#   core/hw/sh4/dyna/ssa.cpp      const-fold disabled on wasm (BOOT-CRITICAL)
#   core/hw/sh4/sh4_mem.cpp       smc_mark_range at the 3 DMA/block chokepoints
#   core/hw/maple/maple_cfg.cpp   VMU on bus 0 expansion slot A1
#   core/hw/aica/sgc_if.cpp       0021 disabled-channel hoist
#   core/rend/TexCache.{cpp,h}    0018 wasm VRAM source hash + RTT exclusion
#   core/rend/gles/{gles.cpp,gles.h,gltex.cpp}  0017 mobile precision/FBO
#   shell/libretro/libretro.cpp   flycast_set_fog / flycast_set_modvol, defined
#                                 in a CORE TU (the bridge's config::Option
#                                 layout differs — see the note in that hunk)
#
